                ],
            ]
        ],
    ],
];</pre>
The <strong>FileWriter</strong> key is optional, otherwise the writers array would be enumerative instead of associative.

The writer <strong>name</strong> key is a developer-provided name for that writer, the writer name key is <strong>mandatory</strong>.

The writer priority key is not affecting the errors that are written, it is a way to organize writers, for example:
<ul>
 	<li>1 - FILE</li>
 	<li>2 - SQL</li>
 	<li>3 - E-mail</li>
</ul>
It is the most important to write in the file, the sql or e-mail are more probably fail because the servers can be external and offline, the file is on the same server.

The writer priority key is optional.

To write into a file the key <strong>stream</strong> must be present in the <strong>writer options</strong> array. This is required only if writing into streams/files.

