<h2>(Optional) Configuring the Filters</h2>
A <em>filter</em> prevents a message from being written to the log. (from <a href="https://zendframework.github.io/zend-log/filters/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">zend-log filters documentation</a>)

As per <a href="https://www.php-fig.org/psr/psr-3/#5-psrlogloglevel" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PSR-3 document</a>.

The log levels are: <strong>emergency (0)</strong>, <strong>alert (1)</strong>, <strong>critical (2)</strong>, <strong>error (3)</strong>, <strong>warn (4)</strong>, <strong>notice (5)</strong>, <strong>info (6)</strong>, <strong>debug (7)</strong> (in order of priority/importance)

Although the plain Logger in Zend Log is not fully compatible with PSR-3, it provides a way to log all of these message types.

&nbsp;

Starting from the basic writer configuration, several configurations will be added for extra functionality.

&nbsp;
